---
import InfoLayout from '../layouts/InfoLayout.astro';
---

<InfoLayout
  eyebrow="Tooling"
  title="Notion"
  description="Where this PMO's structured project record actually lives."
>
  <p>
    Every project gets a home in Notion: a project node page, a Steps database, and a Project
    Workbook database. The skills on this site write to those three surfaces directly — never to
    a random doc, and never by rebuilding a project's structure from scratch each time.
  </p>

  <h2>The project node page</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/#tab-intake">Project Overview</a> creates it as a child subpage the first time a PM
    meets with a sponsor, and <a href="/#tab-intake">Project Registry</a> records exactly where
    the other three repositories — Steps database, Project Workbook, Slack channel — live, in a
    "Data Repositories" section on that same page, so nobody has to ask "where does this live"
    twice.
  </p>

  <h2>The Steps database</h2>
  <p>
    See <a href="/deliverables-first/">Deliverables First</a> for why steps are deliverables, not
    tasks.
  </p>

  <h2>The Project Workbook</h2>
  <p>
    Decisions, risks, dependencies, action items, and the odd stray document link all land here as
    tagged rows — most of it arriving through <a href="/#tab-cadence">Slack/Notion Sync</a> and
    <a href="/#tab-cadence">Link Harvest</a>, never by a PM copying things over by hand.
  </p>
</InfoLayout>
